// S-957 (W5-11 U10d2/t2, §2.5, §6.5, §18.1): the candidate of a line break after the `@` of the attribute of an item moves
// the `@` to the line of its name, and nothing is left behind (`clean`, S-253): `@fp(relaxed)` before a function is a right
// declaration. The main position is the `@`, the first token of the form. A file with one unit, so that `clean` looks at
// the whole file.

@   //~ E0020 @1
  fp(relaxed)
pub fn f(x: F32) -> F32 {
  x
}
